{"id":"w445305","name":"Spiced Oysters","author":"Wikibooks Cookbook contributors","source":{"name":"Wikibooks Cookbook","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Spiced_Oysters"},"via":{"name":"Wikibooks","url":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Cookbook:Spiced_Oysters"},"image":"","cuisine":"","country":"","region":"Global","course":"main","protein":"seafood","diet":1,"allergens":548928,"minutes":40,"time":{"prep":15,"cook":25,"passive":0,"passiveWhy":[]},"timeEstimated":true,"servings":"","difficulty":"easy","ingredients":[{"item":"100 oysters","qty":""},{"item":"12 whole cloves","qty":""},{"item":"24 whole allspice","qty":""},{"item":"Mace, to taste","qty":""},{"item":"Cayenne pepper, to taste","qty":""},{"item":"Salt to taste","qty":""},{"item":"1 cup cider vinegar","qty":""}],"steps":["Strain the oyster liquor through a sieve, and put it in a saucepan.","Add the oysters, spices, salt, and cider vinegar.","Place them over a slow fire, and as soon as they boil remove them from the heat.","Pour the oysters into a large bowl, and let cool.","When cooled, cover and store the oysters."],"tags":[],"youtube":"","culture":null,"license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","lifestyle":125,"era":"modern"}